content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, on the raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing vibration is 8.3 mm/s. Using the applicable HF-300 Figure 3 bearing-housing velocity zones, this exceeds the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary and falls within Zone D (7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS): 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. SSP-07 therefore requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart; this immediate-stop condition drives the P1 response.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-housing temperature is 70 C. HF-300 bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface, and the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is at the upper normal limit, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip. It is not above the alarm limit, so SSP-07's temperature-based priority-1 trigger does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. Consequently, the report does not present the manual's 'leakage at shaft seal' symptom, and mechanical-seal replacement is not scoped solely on the basis of this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment - the first manual-listed probable cause for high vibration; no alignment measurements are supplied to confirm or exclude it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear - a manual-listed probable cause for high vibration. The 70 C housing reading is normal and does not itself demonstrate bearing wear or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage - a manual-listed probable cause requiring inspection of the impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation - a manual-listed probable cause for high vibration; check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-114 immediately and keep it stopped. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before work inside the pump or on its seal, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent before line breaking, and obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot the high vibration by checking shaft alignment and checking NPSH for possible cavitation; record the results for diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After isolation and draining, use the back pull-out arrangement for internal inspection; the rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the required lifting controls. Inspect the bearings and impeller for the high-vibration causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair using HF3-512 and HF3-510. Do not replace them solely because of the reported 70 C housing temperature, which is at the normal limit rather than above it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit new casing gasket HF3-120. For reassembly work actually performed, use lightly oiled threads and Table 5 torques: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm if removed; bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if disturbed. If seal gland nuts are disturbed on this serial, tighten the M10 nuts to 25 Nm, not the service bulletin's 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, use a laser alignment tool. Alignment tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular offset 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any restart, notify the reliability engineer. On return to service, maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run dry. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings every week, classify the highest reading using Figure 3 and act on that zone, including stopping immediately if the highest reading is in Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; conditional on inspection requiring the manual's paired bearing replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; conditional on inspection requiring the manual's paired bearing replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on the casing being opened, in which case it must be replaced.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Zone D vibration requires immediate machine stoppage; notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal pump or seal work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional control: if the raw-water transfer line is chemically dosed, provide chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The fault report does not establish the line's dosing status.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pump uses Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge; never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, only if inspection shows that bearing replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician; applicable after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, whereas the manual parts list and Table 5 specify component seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, below the bulletin range, so the bulletin's explicit below-serial rule governs: continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. For this asset, 25 Nm with lightly oiled threads applies, not HF3-450B or 30 Nm. This decision controls any later seal work; it does not itself add seal replacement to the current scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 8.3 mm/s reading an RMS vibration-velocity measurement? Figure 3's limits are specifically in mm/s RMS, while the fault report does not state the RMS basis (C07).",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading? The manual requires measurements on both bearing housings every week and classification of the highest reading (C06).",
    "What are the alignment measurements, bearing and impeller inspection findings, and NPSH/cavitation results? These are needed to establish the actual cause and confirm whether the conditional bearings or additional parts are required. No NPSH acceptance value or detailed NPSH-check method is supplied (C09, C10).",
    "Is the raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? If it is, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory under SSP-07 (C15).",
    "If seal or sleeve work is later added, what shaft-sleeve scoring acceptance limit applies to serial HF3-20500? The manual requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical limit; SB-2026-014's 0.1 mm instruction is within its serial HF3-22000-and-above scope and should not be assumed for this pump (C10, C13).",
    "What labour should be allowed for initial diagnostics, NPSH checking and bearing/impeller inspection? The standard-time table covers mechanical-seal replacement, paired bearing replacement and laser alignment, but not these diagnostic and inspection activities (C09, C12)."
  ]
}
